# CODE STATE QUERY — code recognition is evidence, not an answer.
#
# The engine already evaluates assignments and ++ inside function bodies.  The
# missing abstraction is a mixed input made of an inline statement trace plus a
# question about one resulting binding.  The nonce cue proves that the boundary
# and intent grow from one live KB fact, without rebuilding.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the exact conversational stimulus is evaluated]
> i=0; i++; quanto vale i
< 1.
> i=0; i++; what is i
< 1.

[test state evaluation composes existing statement mechanics]
> total=3; total += 4; what is the final value of total
< 7.
> a=2; b=5; a++; what is b
< 5.
> int x=4; x *= 3; what is x
< 12.

[test an update without an initial binding is not fabricated]
!timeout 2
> i++; what is i
<! 1.
!timeout 1

[test a new state-question cue grows and ablates at runtime]
> z=2; z++; final register z
<! 3.
!assert segment_role(query, "final register")
> z=2; z++; final register z
< 3.
!forget segment_role(query, "final register")
> z=2; z++; final register z
<! 3.
